# Copy to `.env` at the repository root and fill in. That file is gitignored.
#
#   cp .env.example .env && chmod 600 .env
#   python -m qbs.agent --check
#
# `qbs.agent` reads this file on import, so the CLI, the dashboard and a
# notebook all pick it up with nothing further to do.
#
# A real environment variable ALWAYS wins over a line here, so
# `GOOGLE_API_KEY=... python -m qbs.agent ...` overrides the file for one run.
#
# Syntax is deliberately small: KEY=value, one per line, `#` starts a comment
# only at the beginning of a line, and a matching pair of surrounding quotes
# is stripped. No `$VAR` interpolation and no multi-line values -- export
# those from your shell instead.

# --- required for the LLM analyst ----------------------------------------
# https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# GEMINI_API_KEY is accepted too; Google's own docs use both names.
GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# --- the kill switches ----------------------------------------------------
# One per thing that can spend, and no master over them. Leave all three
# alone and you get: headlines from Tavily and DuckDuckGo, no Gemini call
# anywhere until you type in the chat.
#
# Only an explicit off-word means "off" -- 0, false, no, off, none, disabled.
# ANY other non-empty value reads as ON, so a half-remembered
# `QBS_DISABLE_CHAT=disable` stops the spending rather than quietly leaving
# it running.

# The News tab's Gemini read. OFF UNLESS YOU SET THIS TO 0 -- the only
# switch here whose default is the disabled position, because it is the only
# thing that would spend on page load without anybody pressing anything.
# The headlines show either way; this is just the model's read of them.
# QBS_DISABLE_NEWS_ANALYSIS=0

# Fetching the headlines at all. On by default: that is a web search, free on
# DuckDuckGo and a credit on Tavily, not an LLM call. Set it to stop the
# News tab reaching the internet entirely. Ignored while the analysis above
# is on, since there is nothing to analyse without it.
# QBS_DISABLE_NEWS_READ=1

# The Analyst tab's chat. On by default -- it spends only when you type.
QBS_DISABLE_CHAT=1

# RETIRED: QBS_DISABLE_ANALYST. It used to be the master over all three and
# is read by nothing now. If it is still in your .env, `--check` and the
# dashboard will say so rather than let it look like it is holding your bill
# down. The news read is QBS_DISABLE_NEWS_ANALYSIS; the chat is
# QBS_DISABLE_CHAT.

# --- the model ------------------------------------------------------------
# One model for everything: the news read follows QBS_GEMINI_MODEL unless
# QBS_SUMMARY_MODEL is also set. Set both to split them again.
QBS_GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash

# CHECK THIS NAME BEFORE YOU TRUST IT. Model IDs move faster than this repo,
# and a wrong one fails as a 404 several layers inside LangChain. Run:
#
#     python -m qbs.agent --models
#
# It lists what this key can actually serve, marks the configured one, and
# warns if it is missing from the list. If gemini-3.5-flash is not there, put
# whatever IS there on the line above.

# Thinking budget, CHAT only. -1 lets the model decide, 0 turns thinking off,
# a positive number caps it in tokens. The accepted range is model-specific;
# the API rejects a bad one rather than this file guessing.
# QBS_THINKING_BUDGET=-1

# Split the two roles again by uncommenting this. Worth knowing why you might:
# the chat reasons over tool output turn after turn and re-sends its
# transcript each time (~17x the news panel's tokens), while the news read is
# one call a day over ~30 headlines (~73k tokens a month, pennies at any
# price). Different volumes, so they can justify different models.
# QBS_SUMMARY_MODEL=gemini-2.5-pro

# Better web search than the keyless DuckDuckGo default, and it costs money.
# Set this AND `pip install tavily-python`; qbs.agent.news then prefers it.
TAVILY_API_KEY=

# --- when the dashboard fetches by itself ----------------------------------
# One automatic fetch a day, at this wall-clock time in this timezone, and at
# no other hour. Everything else is Refresh now.
QBS_FETCH_AT=15:00
QBS_FETCH_TZ=Asia/Hong_Kong
#
# Any UTC+8 zone behaves identically (Singapore, Taipei, Shanghai) -- none of
# them observe daylight saving, so 15:00 stays 15:00 while New York moves by
# an hour twice a year. The default is eleven hours after the previous US
# close, so the tape has long settled.
#
# This is a GATE, not a scheduler. Streamlit runs code when something
# interacts with it and at no other time, so the fetch happens on the first
# page load at or after 15:00. Leave the app shut all afternoon and no fetch
# happens that day -- which costs only freshness, since the download is the
# full history each time and the next day's slot picks up both. A missed slot
# is NOT collected late: opening at 09:00 the next morning will not start a
# download, because "at 15:00, manual otherwise" is the rule.
#
# For a download that runs whether or not anyone is looking, you want cron or
# Windows Task Scheduler, not a dashboard -- a dashboard nobody has open is
# not running.

# --- where the US universe comes from --------------------------------------
# Which provider supplies the ~2,600-name US universe for the market tab.
#   finviz       (default) the screener scrape, ~120 paginated requests
#   tradingview  the scanner, one POST -- needs `pip install tradingview-screener`
#
# Not a faster copy of the same universe: the two apply the same rules to
# different listings databases and will not agree on the last hundred names,
# so breadth counts MOVE when you switch. Worth doing deliberately, which is
# why there is no automatic failover between them. The tab names the source
# that produced the numbers.
#
# The momentum rule does not change either way. The 63-session quarterly gain
# is computed from prices in qbs.breadth, not read off a screener column.
# QBS_UNIVERSE_SOURCE=tradingview

# --- watchlist (the DASHBOARD's) -------------------------------------------
# Names to rank beside the book without letting the book buy them. The
# dashboard's Daily picks tab shows a row per name: a constituent (GOOGL) at
# the rank it already has, anything outside the index (TSM) interpolated into
# the same ranking. The sidebar box seeds itself from this and stays
# editable, so this is a starting list rather than a setting. Comma or space
# separated; blank turns it off.
# QBS_DASH_WATCHLIST=TSM,GOOGL
#
# NOT `QBS_WATCHLIST`, on purpose. That is the live runner's watchlist, it
# lives in deploy/docker/.env, and it decides what goes into
# var/watchlist_log.csv on the trading host. Two names and no fallback
# between them, so that adding a name to look at a chart cannot change what
# the runner logs -- and so a host running both does not hand one list to
# two programs. Nothing in the dashboard reads QBS_WATCHLIST.

# Nothing else in this package needs a key. Prices come from Yahoo via
# yfinance, and the Interactive Brokers credentials for live trading live in
# deploy/docker/.env instead -- a different file, on the trading host only.
